            acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Layer splitting adds overhead from inter-GPU communication, and its size depends on interconnect, engine, context length and batch size. This page does not publish a measured figure for two RTX 4090s on 70B. It is usually much faster than CPU offloading, and a single 4090 cannot hold a 70B model at Q4 at all.' },
